-- int-tests-consistency.l4: the cross-group consistency register, as assertions.  Each section pins one question that two or more
-- groups answered, on the same facts, so that the register in NOTES.md (section "The cross-group consistency register") is
-- checked and not only asserted.  Where the groups answer differently, both answers are asserted, each in its own group's terms, and
-- the section says which text of the Law gives each.  Expected values were decided from the Hebrew text and the readings the groups
-- recorded in their FRAGMENTs, before this module was run (see expectations.md).

§ `Tests: the cross-group consistency register`

§§ `Q1. Is a licence in force?  Group 1 (s.10) and group 2 (ss.8, 9) read the same three register fields`

`Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1)

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      licence IS A Licence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two groups agree that the licence is in force or not on` day `for` licence MEANS
    (`the licence is in force on` licence day) EQUALS ((`s 8 — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day) AND NOT `s 10 — the licence is out of force by reason of section 10 on the day` licence day)

`days around a revocation and a suspension in 2028` MEANS LIST YMD 2028 2 28, YMD 2028 2 29, YMD 2028 3 1, YMD 2028 3 31, YMD 2028 4 1, YMD 2028 4 2, YMD 2028 4 30, YMD 2028 5 1, YMD 2028 5 2, YMD 2031 1 31, YMD 2031 2 1, YMD 2031 2 2
`a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it revoked on` (YMD 2028 5 1)
`a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 1 April 2028` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it suspended from` (YMD 2028 3 1) `until` (JUST (YMD 2028 4 1))
`a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it suspended from` (YMD 2028 3 1) `until` NOTHING
#ASSERT all (GIVEN day YIELD `the two groups agree that the licence is in force or not on` day `for` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028`) `days around a revocation and a suspension in 2028`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN day YIELD `the two groups agree that the licence is in force or not on` day `for` `a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 1 April 2028`) `days around a revocation and a suspension in 2028`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN day YIELD `the two groups agree that the licence is in force or not on` day `for` `a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end`) `days around a revocation and a suspension in 2028`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN day YIELD `the two groups agree that the licence is in force or not on` day `for` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026`) `days around a revocation and a suspension in 2028`
-- The edges, stated: a revocation takes effect on the day recorded (both groups, forks F27 and FV6); a suspension runs from its first to its last day, both inside (IL s.8).
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 4 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 1 April 2028` (YMD 2028 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 1 April 2028` (YMD 2028 4 1)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `a licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 1 April 2028` (YMD 2028 4 2)
-- Both groups' alternatives (the effect the day after) agree with each other on the revocation.
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day, the revocation taking effect the day after the day recorded` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day, the revocation taking effect the day after the day recorded` `a licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 2)

§§ `Q2. Does the first day of a period belong to it?  The conventions, group by group, on the days that tell them apart`

-- A status that BEGINS on E (a licence granted, an authorisation granted, a term of office, a text of regulations): E itself is a day of the status in groups 1, 2, 4, 5 and 8.
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` (YMD 2026 1 31)
-- ... and group 2's own alternative begins the day after, the convention of the vendored module.
#ASSERT NOT `s 8 (validity begins the day after the grant) — the licence` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `is within its period of validity on` (YMD 2026 2 1)
-- Group 5: an authorisation granted on 1.1.2026 for 30 days runs on 1.1.2026 and on 31.1.2026, not on 31.12.2025 or 1.2.2026.
`an instrument granted on 1 January 2026 for 30 days` MEANS `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` WITH
    `granted on` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the period fixed in the instrument, if it fixes one` IS JUST (`a number of days fixed in the instrument` 30)
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `under` `an instrument granted on 1 January 2026 for 30 days`
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `under` `an instrument granted on 1 January 2026 for 30 days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `under` `an instrument granted on 1 January 2026 for 30 days`
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 2 1) `under` `an instrument granted on 1 January 2026 for 30 days`
-- Group 4: a term of four years from an appointment on 16.7.2025 ends on 16.7.2029 (the anniversary is inside, like group 2's five years).
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 11: public representative` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2029 7 16)
-- Group 1: a suspension of at most three years from 1.3.2026 may end on 1.3.2029 (the anniversary), not on 2.3.2029.
GIVEN lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)`
`a suspension from 1 March 2026 to` lastDay MEANS `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
    `the measure` IS `suspend the licence`
    `the grounds` IS `Grounds under section 10(a)` WITH
        `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information` IS FALSE
        `a condition for the grant ceased to hold` IS FALSE
        `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)` IS FALSE
        `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS TRUE
        `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded` IS FALSE
        `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property` IS FALSE
    `the consultation of the Council` IS `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS JUST (`Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` WITH `begins on` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `ends on` IS JUST lastDay)
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`a suspension from 1 March 2026 to` (YMD 2029 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`a suspension from 1 March 2026 to` (YMD 2029 3 2))
-- Group 3: the "last year of validity" is counted BACKWARDS from the last day and leaves out the anniversary of that day (the module's convention): for a temporary licence granted 1.12.2025 to 1.12.2026, group 2 has it in force on 1.12.2025 and group 3's last year starts on 2.12.2025.
`a temporary licence granted on 1 December 2025 and recorded to end on 1 December 2026` MEANS `fixture: a temporary licence held by` `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert` `granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `and recorded to end on` (YMD 2026 12 1)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `a temporary licence granted on 1 December 2025 and recorded to end on 1 December 2026` (YMD 2025 12 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2025 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2025 12 2) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1)
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the day is in the last year of validity` (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 12 1)

§§ `Q3. An act "within N days from E" (group 3, s.16): timely if E is the day or later and the day is not after the last day`

`a change on 1 March 2026 notified on` day MEANS `Change in the application particulars` WITH
    `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS TRUE
    `the day of the change` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS FALSE
    `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS FALSE
    `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS JUST day
-- IL s.10(a): 30 days from 1.3.2026 end on 31.3.2026.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`a change on 1 March 2026 notified on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`a change on 1 March 2026 notified on` (YMD 2026 3 31)) `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`a change on 1 March 2026 notified on` (YMD 2026 4 1)) `fixture: no day of rest at all`

-- Group 6 (after its review): the same convention for s.48.  A payment demand delivered 2.6.2027: 30 days from it end on 2.7.2027 (IL s.10(a)); a payment on the day of delivery, or on any day to 2.7.2027, is within the period; 3.7.2027 is not; 1.6.2027 (before the demand) is not.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 2) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 7 3) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 48 — the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `is within the period for payment that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`

-- Group 6 again, s.53(a): a warning delivered 3.3.2027; 30 days from it end on 2.4.2027 (March has 31 days: 28 days to 31.3, 2 more); a request on the day of delivery, or on 2.4.2027, is within the period; 3.4.2027 is not.
`a warning delivered on 3 March 2027` MEANS `Administrative warning` WITH
    `the violator` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `the listed violation the warning concerns` IS `work with no licence at all`
    `delivered on` IS YMD 2027 3 3
    `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
    `tells the violator to stop the breach` IS TRUE
    `warns of a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation` IS TRUE
    `states the violator's right to ask for cancellation under section 53` IS TRUE
    `cancelled under section 53` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a warning delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` NOTHING `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 2) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a warning delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` NOTHING `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`
#ASSERT NOT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 4 3) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a warning delivered on 3 March 2027` `given` NOTHING `with` `fixture: no day of rest at all`

§§ `Q4. Is a lapsed licence a licence?  No, in every group that asks`

-- Group 1 (fork F8): work with a lapsed licence is work with no licence at all (S01).  Group 3 (S18-H): an operator who engages a person whose licence lapsed commits item (5) (S05).
-- Group 3, s.12: the holder of a lapsed licence is not a licensee, so a transfer is no breach; the holder of a licence in force who transfers it breaches s.12.
`a stranger` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "il-stranger", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
#ASSERT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `a stranger` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `a stranger` EMPTY TRUE
-- Group 7 (s.58): a lapsed licensee is not treated as a service electrician (S17).
#ASSERT NOT `the licensee is treated as a service electrician under section 58` EMPTY TRUE

§§ `Q5. "Appropriate to the work": group 1 (s.3(a), items (2)) and group 3 (s.18(a), item (6)) mean the same by it`

-- The oil of maintenance (B.3(3)) on 5 kW and a grade 1 holder: the worker commits item (2) and the operator who engaged her item (6) (S06); wired from the capacity alone, the operator would not (the alternative).
#ASSERT NOT elem `grade 1 licence` (`licence kinds appropriate to the activity on the system` `B.3(3) adding or replacing oil during maintenance` (`fixture: a system of` 5 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"))
#ASSERT elem `grade 1 licence` (`licence kinds that cover a cooling system` (`fixture: a system of` 5 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"))

§§ `Q6. The word "offence": group 2 (s.6(a)(3)), group 4 (s.21) and group 5 (s.30(b)(1)) on the same fact, a conviction for a DISCIPLINARY offence that the authority finds makes the person unfit`

-- s.6(a)(3) says "criminal offence"; s.21 says "criminal or disciplinary"; s.30(b)(1) says only "offence" (group 5 reads it as criminal, fork F-OFFENCE; the alternative counts a disciplinary conviction).
`a record showing a disciplinary conviction only` MEANS `Record of offences` WITH
    `convicted of a criminal offence` IS FALSE
    `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS TRUE
    `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS FALSE
    `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE
`an applicant with only a disciplinary conviction` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `the person` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `of full age` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
    `record of offences` IS `a record showing a disciplinary conviction only`
    `licences held` IS EMPTY
    `certificates held` IS EMPTY
    `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
    `periods of work on cooling systems` IS EMPTY
    `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
    `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` (`fixture: an application by` `an applicant with only a disciplinary conviction` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)) TRUE
`a candidate inspector with only a disciplinary conviction` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` WITH
    `an employee of the Ministry` IS TRUE
    `record of offences` IS `a record showing a disciplinary conviction only`
    `in the Minister's opinion an offence of which the candidate was convicted makes him unfit to serve as an inspector` IS TRUE
    `received the training the Minister directed in the field of the powers he will hold` IS TRUE
    `meets the further conditions of eligibility, if the Minister directed any` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(b) — the candidate may be authorised as an inspector` `a candidate inspector with only a disciplinary conviction`
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(1), counting a conviction for a disciplinary offence too` `a candidate inspector with only a disciplinary conviction`
-- Group 4 takes a conviction of either kind that the appointer finds unfit as a bar to the Council.
`a disciplinary conviction the appointer finds unfit` MEANS `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` WITH
    `the offence, by its nature, severity or circumstances, makes the person unfit to be a member of the Council` IS TRUE
    `the outcome of the proceeding` IS `proceeding ended in a conviction`
#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST `a disciplinary conviction the appointer finds unfit`)

§§ `Q7. Commencement: which provisions wait for it?  Seven conventions on the same day (1.6.2026, before paragraph (2) of s.63(a) has begun for an R134a system)`

-- Group 7: a provision that is not about work on a system has no commencement day in the Law (s.63(a)); the answer is a refusal, and the integrated grant headline is gated on the first commencement day instead.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Law has commenced, for a provision that is not about work on a system, on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- Group 3 gates the duties of ss.12 to 17 on "the Law has commenced for the licensee's work" (fork COM): the same transfer is a breach when the Law has commenced and none when it has not.
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026` `a stranger` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) FALSE
-- Group 2 states no gate; the integrated grant headline is gated on the commencement day only (S01).
-- (On 1.6.2026 the fee has been updated by regulation 3: 284 times 101.25/100 rounds to 288, so the amount paid is 288 and the readings are given.)
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant with the readings on` (`fixture: an application by` (`fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual`) `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) `with the amount paid being` 288 `and the readings being` `fixture: the index readings for the fees`)
-- Group 5: the inspector's powers are used only where the Law has commenced for the work supervised (a field of the occasion); his authorisation is not tied to it.
`an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` MEANS `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST `require name, address and identification`, `require information or a document`, `enter a place to supervise`, `make measurements and tests`, `order measurements and tests kept`, `deal with measurements and tests otherwise`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the inspector may use the power` `an inspector where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `require information or a document`
-- Group 1, ss.5, 10, 11: no commencement input at all: the Registrar's power under s.10(a) is the same answer on every day (S09 uses 2028).

§§ `Q8. "The fee was paid in full" (group 2's input) and regulation 4 (group 8): the semantic difference`

-- Regulation 4 binds only a service for which a fee was fixed.  As made, no fee is fixed for a theoretical exam, so the Training Division is free to allow it with nothing paid, where "the fee was paid in full" would be false.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY
-- As amended a theoretical exam has a fee of 158: 157 does not suffice.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 157 (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 158 (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees`

§§ `Q9. Electrical work on a cooling system: s.58 (a wide gateway) and s.61 (the First Schedule only), group 7, against group 1's definition of "work"`

-- Group 7's two readings differ when "the act is work on a cooling system" is a fact given independently of group 1: s.58 lets the licensee in, s.61 does not (the electrical work is not in accordance with the First Schedule).
#ASSERT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) TRUE FALSE
-- Wired to group 1 (IP4), "work on a cooling system" is an act of a kind the First Schedule lists, so electrical work outside the First Schedule is not work on a cooling system and s.58 does not reach it either: the two readings collapse (S17).

§§ `Q10. Two violations by one person in two capacities (a licensee and an operator)`

-- Dana does unlicensed work (item (1)) and, as an operator, engages Noa with a lapsed licence (item (5), individual): two acts, two references, two violations, each priced on its own (s.55 forbids more than one sanction for ONE act).
`Dana as an operator who engages Noa, whose licence lapsed` MEANS `Situation of one engagement` WITH
    `the operator` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `facts about the operator` IS `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` WITH
        `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS TRUE
        `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS FALSE
    `licences of the engaged person` IS LIST (`fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Noa, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1))
    `the day of the engagement` IS YMD 2030 4 1
    `the cooling system worked on` IS `fixture: a system of` 25 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
    `the activity the act amounts to` IS JUST `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
    `the limits of the item` IS `fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied`
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 18(a) in` `Dana as an operator who engages Noa, whose licence lapsed` `with the reference` "dana-engages-noa" EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`, `the listed violation` IS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`, `reference for the act` IS "dana-engages-noa", `date of the act` IS YMD 2030 4 1)

§§ `Q11. Which function of s.26(a) is a course required under s.17(b)? (group 3, contradiction C10; group 4)`

-- s.26(a)(3) names the extension of validity but not the requirement of a particular course.  If the course is function (3), a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers (procedure followed) can give the advice; if it is function (4), only the Council at a quorate meeting can.
`the subcommittee's delegated advice, procedure followed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` WITH `the Council delegated its powers in the function to the subcommittee` IS TRUE, `the subcommittee proceeded as the procedure fixed by the Council requires` IS JUST TRUE
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`the work of Dana on 11 June 2027 after a course she missed, advice by` consultation MEANS `fixture: training records added to the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026`) `on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`) `being` (LIST `Training record under one licence` WITH
    `the licence the record concerns` IS `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026`
    `the sessions attended` IS EMPTY
    `the courses required under section 17(b)` IS LIST (`int — the course required under section 17(b) by` (`Requirement of a particular course under section 17(b)` WITH
        `the day of the course` IS YMD 2027 6 10
        `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS YMD 2027 5 1
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS TRUE
        `the consultation of the Council about requiring the course` IS consultation
        `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE
        `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS TRUE
        `the licensee attended the course` IS FALSE
        `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS FALSE)))
#ASSERT `int — a licence condition was breached in the situation` (`the work of Dana on 11 June 2027 after a course she missed, advice by` (`int — a consultation on an individual matter whose advice came from` `the subcommittee's delegated advice, procedure followed`))
#ASSERT NOT `int — a licence condition was breached in the situation` (`the work of Dana on 11 June 2027 after a course she missed, advice by` (`int — a consultation on another function whose advice came from` `the subcommittee's delegated advice, procedure followed`))
-- At a quorate meeting of the Council the function does not matter.
#ASSERT `int — a licence condition was breached in the situation` (`the work of Dana on 11 June 2027 after a course she missed, advice by` (`int — a consultation on another function whose advice came from` (`the Council at a meeting` WITH `the meeting` IS `fixture: a meeting with six present including the chair, three for and two against`)))

§§ `Q12. "The same provision" (group 6, s.45(b)) and the items of the Third Schedule that groups 1 and 3 produce`

-- Items (5) and (6) both contravene s.18(a); items (1) and (2) both s.3(a).  An operator who engaged an unlicensed person (item (5)) in 2029 and a wrongly licensed one (item (6)) in 2030 repeats a violation of the same provision (group 6's reading taken); read by item it does not (the alternative).
`Ofek's violation of item (6) on 1 April 2030` MEANS Violation WITH
    `the violator` IS `fixture: Ofek Ltd, a corporation`
    `the listed violation` IS `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
    `reference for the act` IS "ofek-2030"
    `date of the act` IS YMD 2030 4 1
`Ofek's earlier violation of item (5) on 1 June 2029, sanctioned` MEANS `Previous violation` WITH
    `the violator` IS `fixture: Ofek Ltd, a corporation`
    `the listed violation` IS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
    `date of the act` IS YMD 2029 6 1
    `a financial sanction was imposed for it` IS TRUE
    `the violator was convicted for it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` `Ofek's violation of item (6) on 1 April 2030` `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `Ofek's earlier violation of item (5) on 1 June 2029, sanctioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` `Ofek's violation of item (6) on 1 April 2030` `Ofek's earlier violation of item (5) on 1 June 2029, sanctioned`

§§ `Q13. A temporary licence with no recorded last day: group 2's refusal reaches the whole list of kinds, and the wiring does not hide it`

`a temporary licence with no recorded last day` MEANS Licence WITH
    `the holder` IS `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert`
    `the kind of licence` IS `grade 3 licence`
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS TRUE
    `granted on` IS YMD 2025 12 1
    `renewed on` IS EMPTY
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS NOTHING
    `revoked on` IS NOTHING
    `suspended from` IS NOTHING
    `suspended until` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the licence kinds in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) (LIST `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026`, `a temporary licence with no recorded last day`)
#ASSERT `int — the licence kinds in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) (LIST `Dana's licence granted on 1 February 2026`) EQUALS LIST `grade 1 licence`
